🚨 severity: BLOCKING —
🚨 **BLOCKING: CI red on head `eacc8fcd` — the duplication ratchet fails on `js/common/failureAnalyzer.js` (both `crap` runs)**

The CRAP ratchet is green now (`0 regression(s), 0 new over threshold` — the `verdictPayloadOf` fix landed, F1 verified fixed), and unit tests pass — but the job still exits 2 on the **fresh-duplication gate** in both runs ([12:24 run](https://github.com/IstiN/dmtools-agents/actions/runs/42212297477), [12:21 run](https://github.com/IstiN/dmtools-agents/actions/runs/42212108835)):

```text
fresh duplication: js/common/failureAnalyzer.js 1.67% (not pinned in duplication-baseline.json)
duplication ratchet: FAIL — 1 fresh, 0 regressed (1 pinned debt files unchanged)
##[error]Process completed with exit code 2.
```

Reproduced locally with the CI-pinned tool (`IstiN/crap4js@83ee6201`, `duplicates --threshold 1 --exclude "js/unit-tests/**" js ci`) — the clone is the two "newest verdict for this signature" scan loops:

```text
js/common/failureAnalyzer.js:345: clone: 50 tokens / 6 lines, 2 occurrences:
  js/common/failureAnalyzer.js:345-350;  js/common/failureAnalyzer.js:535-540
```

`latestPreClassifierVerdict` (this line, added by this PR) and `latestVerdictForSignature` are token-identical apart from the extra `&& v.source === TRANSIENT_SOURCE` clause. On `origin/main` this file measured **0.00% duplicated** — the PR introduced the file's first clone, and the gate (threshold 1%) fails on any unpinned fresh duplication.

Fix: extract one shared scan and keep both wrappers —

```js
function latestVerdictOf(verdicts, signature, source) {
    var list = verdicts || [];
    var latest = null;
    for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {
        var v = list[i];
        if (v && v.signature === signature && (!source || v.source === source)) latest = v;
    }
    return latest;
}

function latestPreClassifierVerdict(verdicts, signature) {
    return latestVerdictOf(verdicts, signature, TRANSIENT_SOURCE);
}
```

`latestVerdictForSignature` becomes `latestVerdictOf(verdicts, signature, null)`; both call sites and the existing tests keep their semantics (newest match wins, list order). Single loop ⇒ no 50-token clone ⇒ gate green.

⚠️ severity: IMPORTANT —
⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the new regex memo throws `TypeError` (kills the SM tick) for a valid config pattern named like an `Object.prototype` key**

`compiledTransientPattern` caches by `TRANSIENT_PATTERN_CACHE[source] === undefined`. A plain `{}` inherits `Object.prototype`, so a pattern source equal to an inherited own-key (`'constructor'`, `'toString'`, `'valueOf'`, `'hasOwnProperty'`, `'__proto__'`, …) is treated as **already cached**, the inherited value (`Object` function / `Object.prototype`) is returned instead of a RegExp, and `transientPatternMatches`'s `re.test(text)` throws `TypeError: re.test is not a function` — uncaught through `matchesTransientPattern` → `transientPreClassifierVerdict` → `gateBlindRedispatch` → `decideActions`, so the whole SM tick dies.

Verified against this tree (`node -e require('./js/common/failureAnalyzer.js')…`):

```text
pattern=constructor → THROWS: TypeError: re.test is not a function
pattern=__proto__   → THROWS: TypeError: re.test is not a function
pattern=toString    → THROWS: TypeError: re.test is not a function
config validation admits it: ["constructor"]
```

`resolveFailureAnalysisConfig` explicitly **admits** such entries (a non-empty string that compiles as a regex — `'constructor'` compiles fine), so this is a valid-config crash, and the pre-memo code handled it correctly (compiled per call). It also contradicts the fail-safe this function documents ("the loop is never wedged by a bad pattern"). A plausible real trigger: matching `…reading 'toString'`-style crash messages with the bare word.

Fix: make the cache own-key only —

```js
var CACHE = {};
function cachedRe(source) {
    if (typeof source !== 'string' || !source) return null;
    if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(CACHE, source)) {
        var re = null;
        try { re = new RegExp(source, 'i'); } catch (eRegex) { re = null; }
        CACHE[source] = re;
    }
    return CACHE[source];
}
```

(or prefix the keys: `CACHE['p:' + source]`). Please extend the memo test suite with a `'constructor'`/`'toString'` source pinning no-throw + match semantics.

