🚨 severity: BLOCKING —
🚨 **BLOCKING: CI red — CRAP ratchet failure (`crap` check failed on both runs)**

Commit `406e2dc9` fails the `crap` check twice ([run 42212297477](https://github.com/IstiN/dmtools-agents/actions/runs/42212297477/job/127873687256), [run 42212108835](https://github.com/IstiN/dmtools-agents/actions/runs/42212108835/job/127873050000)):

```text
CRAP ratchet failed: CRAP may only decrease.
NEW > 8  js/common/failureAnalyzer.js::verdictPayloadOf: 9
0 regression(s), 1 new over threshold, 0 improvement(s), 0 removed
```

The two `backoffTicks`/`ticksSoFar` ternaries added here push `verdictPayloadOf` from CC 7 to CC 9 (CRAP 9 at full branch coverage) — over `CRAP_THRESHOLD=8`, and the ratchet only accepts decreases. The PR's own acceptance line ("every new function ≤ CRAP threshold 8 at full branch coverage") is contradicted by this function. Unit tests are green (8978 passed in both runs) — only this complexity gate is red, so merge stays blocked until it passes.

Fix: extract the optional/nullable fields into one small shaper so both functions sit at CC ≤ 8 while build and parse keep sharing a single defaults ladder:

```js
function verdictOptionalFieldsOf(record) {
    return {
        confidence: typeof record.confidence === 'number' ? record.confidence : null,
        analyzedAtCount: isPositiveInt(record.analyzedAtCount) ? record.analyzedAtCount : null,
        // gh-1380: the pre-classifier's retry-backoff window — absent
        // (null) on every AI-analyzer verdict and on backoff-off stamps.
        backoffTicks: isPositiveInt(record.backoffTicks) ? record.backoffTicks : null,
        ticksSoFar: isPositiveInt(record.ticksSoFar) ? record.ticksSoFar : null
    };
}
```

Then keep `verdictPayloadOf` on the plain fields (`signature`, `classification`, `suspected_root_cause`, `evidence`, `suggested_fix`, `at`, `source`) and copy the four optional fields from the helper explicitly (GraalJS-safe: no spread). That drops `verdictPayloadOf` to CC 6 and the helper to CC 5, and the CRAP ratchet goes green again.

